<p>Also one outbreak is &quot;unscheduled&quot;? That's a creepy word to throw in there.</p>
<p>Edit: <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">There's a small incongruence. First you say &quot;No non-anomalous transmission method of SCP-2559 is known.&quot; then later on &quot;Following the return to Site-91, 12 further researchers were found to have become infected. The spread of rumours within the facility lead to rapid spread of infection among site staff.&quot; Surely having a virus spread new infection by rumor should be considered anomalous? From a medical point of view, becoming infected is very different from displaying symptoms. Symptoms are ways we can see issues, but they are not the issues themselves. I'm just a bit confused by the mixed use of the words.</span></p>
