<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I think this is a sentient being who inadvertedly ingested/became things starting with vi (vision-&gt;virus-&gt;vitiligio). These things may come directly from books, or they could come from the minds of the infected. I don't necessarily think it is trying to harm humans, although there's no evidence for or against. What I do think is that it is trying to survive, and possibly stop spreading or harming people. To do that it needs to get rid of concepts it internalized. Anyway, what is the one organization currently dedicated to keeping it alive - ie subjects alive? That is why it is actively trying to reach out to the Foundation (&quot;sur2559ng&quot;, creepy logo mark). Maybe this being doesn't like dying any more than the rest of us?</p>
<p>Also, I'm thinking the pile of books might not necessarily be the being collecting knowledge to ingest - it can't control people directly or you'd have a doctor telling everyone they're infected. I think it may be the people getting ready for a good ol' book-burning. Maybe they thought it would cure them - maybe it would have! It is, after all, both a literal and theoretical destruction of an idea/concept.</p>
